     "<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">If there are 2 latent variables and 1 observed variable in the mediation\r\ntest.</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Latent variable 1= A     This has 4 items</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Latent variable 2= B  (mediation\r\nvariable)    This has 3 items</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Observed variable = C (one item)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Can a mediation model be defined as A</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Wingdings\">à</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">C,    A</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Wingdings\">à</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">B,      B</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Wingdings\">à</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">C?</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Kind regards, Veysel</span></p>"
